response:
The retrieved articles say the chain was:

- a baby had contracted cholera from another source;
- the baby’s cloth nappy was washed and its waste water drained into an old cesspit;
- that cesspit had begun to leak faecal bacteria;
- the cesspit was only about 3 feet (0.9 m) from the Broad Street well/pump.

So the water became associated with the outbreak because sewage contamination from the leaking cesspit reached the well near the Broad Street pump.
